  "difficulty": "Easy",
  "description": "<div>\n<p>An array digits spells a nonnegative integer, most significant digit first. Return the digit array representing one more than that integer. Carrying past the first digit may make the returned array longer; do not rely on converting the full array to a fixed-width integer.</p>\n<p><strong>Example 1:</strong></p>\n<pre><strong>Input:</strong> digits = [1,2,3]\n<strong>Output:</strong> [1,2,4]\n<strong>Explanation:</strong> Only the final digit changes.</pre>\n<p><strong>Example 2:</strong></p>\n<pre><strong>Input:</strong> digits = [9,9]\n<strong>Output:</strong> [1,0,0]\n<strong>Explanation:</strong> A carry creates a new leading digit.</pre>\n<p><strong>Example 3:</strong></p>\n<pre><strong>Input:</strong> digits = [0]\n<strong>Output:</strong> [1]\n<strong>Explanation:</strong> One more than zero is one.</pre>\n<p><strong>Constraints:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>1 &lt;= digits.length &lt;= 100</code>.</li>\n<li>Each digit is an integer from 0 through 9.</li>\n<li>The first digit is nonzero unless the entire array is <code>[0]</code>.</li>\n</ul>\n</div>",
